{"type": "result", "session_id": "20260930_143032_eb8428", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Email 1: Subject \u2014 Reduce cloud workstation costs without losing capability\n\nMorgan,\n\nYour engineers rely on cloud-hosted workstations for CAD and simulation. That model works when connectivity is reliable and data stays in the office. It struggles on site visits and adds a recurring monthly bill to every seat.\n\nA mobile workstation that handles AI tasks locally can lower that cloud spend while giving your team access to client files offline. You keep control of project data on devices you manage directly.\n\nThe Aurora 14 runs open-weight language models up to about 30 billion parameters on device. Engineers can process drawings and project files without sending them to the cloud.\n\nI will share how this impacts your total cost of ownership next week. No commitment required.\n\nCall to action: Reply \"yes\" if you want the cost comparison.\n\n\n---\n\nEmail 2: Subject \u2014 Cloud-first teams still need local power\n\nMorgan,\n\nYou asked why powerful laptops matter when you already pay for cloud workstations. The answer lies in what happens when connectivity fails or security policies tighten.\n\nThe Aurora 14 brings the compute to the engineer. Its Helix H9 processor has an integrated NPU rated at 60 TOPS. With 64 GB of memory or more, it runs open-weight language models up to about 30 billion parameters locally. Client drawings and project files never leave the device unless you authorize it.\n\nFor site visits with unreliable connectivity, engineers stay productive. For fleet management, you add one device type with 3-year on-site, next-business-day service standard. Memory and storage are user-upgradeable through two SO-DIMM slots and two M.2 slots.\n\nThis complements your cloud strategy rather than replacing it.\n\nCall to action: Reply with your current monthly cloud workstation cost per seat.\n\n\n---\n\nEmail 3: Subject \u2014 15 minutes before Q1 budget closes\n\nMorgan,\n\nYour hardware and software budget cycle closes at the end of Q1. Anything not approved by then waits a year.\n\nWe can walk through how the Aurora 14 fits into your existing cloud-first strategy. I will show the starting price of $2,899 for the base configuration, warranty options extendable to 5 years, and how the 14-inch form factor (starting at 1.65 kg) supports field work.\n\nAvailability is Q4, so ordering now positions you for deployment when your new cycle opens.\n\nNo sales pitch. Just facts on total cost, security controls like TPM 2.0 and self-healing BIOS, and fleet manageability.\n\nCall to action: Book 15 minutes on my calendar here: [insert calendar link]", "tokens": {"input": 4666, "output": 558, "total": 5224, "cache_read": 0, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 8641, "timestamp": 1790803841912}